                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This isn't really a platformer (you don't have much control over the bombs) but it's more like The Incredible Machine or Lemmings. The bombs enter the level from a set point and you have a handful of tools you can use to send the bombs where you want them to go. Gravity is enough to get them started but when they stall out, they roll into each other and explode, which means the bomb in front gets a boost from the bomb behind it. This can create some very interesting and surprising situations, especially on levels where you have more tools available. (What tools you have varies from level to level.)\n\nUltimately the goal is to blow up all the rocks on the level that have gems in them so you can collect money from them and move onto the next level. As you beat levels you get experience points that help you unlock other kinds of bombs that have special abilities, as well as upgrades for bombs you already have.\n\nBecause it's a puzzle game, there are levels when you're probably going to get stuck. There are hints available for every level you can activate if you're at that point where it's going from fun to frustrating, but I haven't had that happen. (Yet.)\n\n+Pros: Lots of levels with lots of possible solutions. A pretty concise tutorial and good controls. \n\n-Cons: You cannot move tools around while bombs are moving. I understand why they did this but there are moments when it can slow down the pace of the game till you learn how it works.",
